A||||9||sqoach||Radiator's out, now what?||||5||
Z||000000||sqoach||04-08-2001||05:16 PM||||Well I got the radiator out today. (I figured I should check the radiator after everything else I've checked (thanks chat people  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">))<P>Anyway, from what I can see, it doesn't look too bad. The top tube is a little bent, but not bad. Doesn't seem like it would clog up. I did talk to a mechanic the other day. He's a pretty nice guy and seems to know what he's talking about. I told him everything that's happened. (member's following my story know what I mean) Then he told me that if some of the tubes are pinched together, it would cause the water to not flow straight and smooth. If it's pinched in the middle, there would be 2 streams of water from that tube. This would cause the two streams to cross and stir, making foam or bubbles. This sound logical?<P>Anyway, I'm not sure if I should buy a new radiator or what. I just want to get this problem solved. Thanks for reading and give me some advice if you can.<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>           <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach2.JPG">  <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily overheating)||||reg||5
Z||000001||DavidHenshaw||04-08-2001||05:35 PM||||Take it to a good radiator shop and have it tested. If its not servicable they should be able to tell you.<P>Dave<P>86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||sqoach||04-08-2001||10:32 PM||||I'm planning on taking it to a radiator shop tomorrow. But I took a better look at it, and it doesn't seem to be in bad shape at all. In fact, it looks really good for being 15 years old (if it's the stock one) and from what I can see in the inside, it looks good too. (but I couldn't see much cuz it's hard to see, ya know)<P>Is it possible for the inside to be really crappy, and the outside still look pretty darn good?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Rex||04-08-2001||10:51 PM||||since you have it out a radiator shop will boil it out and pressure test it. Also will check the flow rate for a minimal charge. I can't find your original topic and am guessing you are having a heating problem. If so what have you checked to date?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cooter||04-09-2001||12:48 AM||||My 3.4 has always run a little warm, even with a 180 thermostat and vented hood. I developed a sudden coolant leak from the left tank on the radiator, so I decided to strip the tanks of a thin core 4 cyl. radiator and put them on my radiator. The crap that was inside that thing was horrible! The lower half of the radiator was completly stopped up and the rest was about half way stopped up. It is amazing the thing was not boiling over all the time. After a couple of hours with some strong cleaner and some stiff wire, I got the passages clear on all but the top and bottom. Now, no more high temps. My advice- get it cleaned!||||reg||1
Z||000005||sqoach||04-09-2001||01:31 PM||||Anyone have some price estimates they'd like to share? Like about how much it would cost to get it boiled out and all that. I know a new radiator at the FieroStore is $179. That would kill my piggy bank. But if it's gonna cost close to the same, I'd just assume it would be better to get a new one.||||reg||1
Z||000006||1988LRC||04-09-2001||04:04 PM||||the radiator shop here charges $60 to clean, rod, and pressure test if you need a new core or tank then thats extra||||reg||1
Z||000007||Archie||04-09-2001||07:58 PM||||Just in case you want one.<P>I have like 30 or 40 good stock used Fiero radiators for $40 + shipping each. <P>All of these are guaranteed to be good or free replacement.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000008||fiero56||04-09-2001||11:35 PM||||I'm in the same situation Sqoach.<P>My 2.8 has always run hot, I have to run 180 degree 'stat in any weather over 60F or it overheats, unless I constantly run the fan. <P>I ordered a new radiator from AutoZone today for $140, will be here Tuesday. I pulled my old one tonight. Like you, I couldn't see inside very well, but am hoping this new one helps keep the car cool. I know jack about radiators, but the one I ordered is a "3 row" radiator. I don't know what that means, but I hope it's good. Will find out tommorrow if it solves the problem.||||reg||1
Z||000009||sqoach||04-09-2001||11:43 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Archie:<BR><B>Just in case you want one.<P>I have like 30 or 40 good stock used Fiero radiators for $40 + shipping each. <P>All of these are guaranteed to be good or free replacement.<P>Archie</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey thanks Archie. I might take you up on that. I'm getting mine checked out down at a local shop. Just took it down there earlier today. They'll tell me what's up tomorrow.||||reg||1
